  "body": "Privately positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac and overlooking a peaceful reserve, 2/26 Huron Street offers a rare sense of space and seclusion in the heart of Takapuna.\r\n\r\nWrapped in a leafy bush outlook, this brick and cedar home has been designed with family living in mind. The flexible floorplan features four bedrooms, two bathrooms, generous living areas and a dedicated office – providing plenty of room for growing families, guests and working from home.\r\n\r\nSkylights draw natural light into the heart of the home, while the living spaces connect effortlessly with an expansive deck and private garden, creating an inviting setting for entertaining, summer barbecues or simply relaxing in the sun.\r\n\r\nOutside, there's lawn for children and pets to enjoy, with established greenery enhancing the home's privacy and tranquil outlook. A double garage and additional off-street parking add another layer of convenience – particularly valuable this close to central Takapuna.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's the location.\r\n\r\nTakapuna Beach, cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities are all within easy reach. Start the morning with a walk or swim at the beach, meet friends for coffee in town, or enjoy everything this vibrant coastal community has to offer.\r\n\r\nFamilies will also appreciate access to highly regarded local schooling, with the property zoned for Westlake Girls High School, Takapuna Normal Intermediate and Takapuna Grammar School.\r\n\r\nPublic transport and motorway connections are conveniently close, making commuting to the city and getting around the North Shore straightforward.\r\n\r\nOffering the space and flexibility of a genuine family home, together with privacy, a peaceful reserve outlook and the coastal lifestyle Takapuna is renowned for, 2/26 Huron Street is an opportunity well worth discovering.",
